            "created_at": "2025-08-01T19:45:05.590883+00:00",
            "notes": "Round 3 is where things start to heat up. A 2nd boop means a significant amount more healing output and crowd control.\n\nOn maps where the point is located at the top of stairs (Like lijang), you can use this to prevent a team from even getting to the point early in the round by frustratingly booping them back down the stairs. This often leads to an easy first cap on a control point map. Also very useful for double booping off maps (Like ruins). \n\nThe most important item at this point is Lumerico Fusion drive. This allows each boop to not only heal, but generate you armor. This significantly improves your survivability.\n\nWith your newfound double boop, you also have a lot more freedom to take duels and go for backline picks. Your gameplay loop is no longer sitting with your team healing but more of a back and forth.\n\nPick a target and rush them in the backline. This is usually going to be a support or non-cassidy DPS. Your goal isn't necessarily to get the kill, but to disrupt their teams focus. You want to get a pick or have at least 2 of their team turn to look at you, giving your team the advantage on the front line. \n\nAs soon as you've used 2 boops, amp speed/heal your way out of there and get back to your team regardless of whether or not you got the kill. If you time it well, when you get back to your team, your amp should still be healing and a boop (Maybe 2) are off cooldown to burst heal your team before spamming and waiting for your amp cooldown to be nearly up and then you repeat the cycle. \n\nFor items, you are focusing on Luimerico then getting your ability power as high as possible. A bit of cooldown reduction is nice as well, but outside of the addition of the single epic, your items remain mostly the same.",
